  "minutes": 9,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Chapter 1 planted the key: **reciprocal exponents cancel**. To solve x^(3/2) = 8, raise both sides to the power 2/3: x = 8^(2/3) = (∛8)² = **4**. One move undoes the exponent — no radical juggling required.",
      "figure": "re-reciprocal-cancel"
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Undo a unit fraction.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "expLogExplore",
        "mode": "exponential",
        "x": 3,
        "targetBase": 2,
        "startBase": 1.5,
        "showMirror": false,
        "prompt": "x^(1/3) = 2 says the cube root of x is 2. Slide the base to 2 and read base³ — that reverses the root.",
        "successFeedback": "2³ = 8, so x = 8. Raising BOTH sides of x^(1/3) = 2 to the power 3 undoes the fractional exponent — the widget shows the undoing directly: cube the 2 that the root already gave you.",
        "lowFeedback": "base³ is still under 8.",
        "highFeedback": "base³ has passed 8."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Check the reciprocal arithmetic: (x^(3/2))^(2/3) = x^(3/2 · 2/3) = x¹. And evaluate the other side the easy way: 8^(2/3) roots first — ∛8 = 2, then 2² = 4. Verify the answer forward: 4^(3/2) = (√4)³ = 2³ = 8. ✓",
      "figure": "re-reciprocal-check"
    },
    {
      "id": "k1",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "The full move.",
      "conceptTag": "re-power-solve",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "x^(3/2) = 27 → x = 27^(2/3) = (∛27)² = 9.",
        "Reciprocal power 2/3; root first: ∛27 = 3, then square."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "exactNumberLab",
        "prompt": "Solve x^(3/2) = 27.",
        "task": "rationalExponentSolve",
        "values": [],
        "rexP": 3,
        "rexQ": 2,
        "rexRhs": 27,
        "answerMode": "numeric",
        "tolerance": 0,
        "numericErrors": [
          {
            "value": 3,
            "feedback": "3 is ∛27 — finish the reciprocal power: square it, x = 9."
          },
          {
            "value": 18,
            "feedback": "The exponent 2/3 roots-then-powers — it never multiplies: 27 · 2/3 = 18 is the wrong move."
          }
        ],
        "choices": [],
        "authoredStages": [],
        "requiredStageKeys": [],
        "requiredExplorations": 1,
        "explorationFeedback": "Inspect the required exact-number states before checking.",
        "fallbackFeedback": "x = 27^(2/3) = 3² = 9; check 9^(3/2) = 27. ✓",
        "successFeedback": "x = 27^(2/3) = 3² = 9; check 9^(3/2) = 27. ✓"
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "a2-radicals",
        "form": "re-power-solve__numeric"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Choose the undo power.",
      "widget": {
