        "prompt": "To solve x^(2/5) = 4, raise both sides to which power?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "o1",
            "label": "5/2",
            "correct": true,
            "feedback": "Right — 2/5 · 5/2 = 1: x = 4^(5/2) = (√4)⁵ = 32."
          },
          {
            "id": "o2",
            "label": "2/5",
            "correct": false,
            "feedback": "Repeating the same power gives x^(4/25) — the UNDO is the reciprocal, 5/2."
          },
          {
            "id": "o3",
            "label": "−2/5",
            "correct": false,
            "feedback": "A negative power takes a reciprocal of the VALUE — flipping the fraction (5/2) is what cancels."
          },
          {
            "id": "o4",
            "label": "5",
            "correct": false,
            "feedback": "5 alone leaves x² = 4⁵ — the reciprocal needs both parts: 5/2."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
